            <ArticleTitle>Production and Characteristics of a Novel Xylose- and Alkali-tolerant GH 43 β-xylosidase from Penicillium oxalicum for Promoting Hemicellulose Degradation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11600</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/s41598-017-11573-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>β-xylosidase is a pivotal enzyme for complete degradation of xylan in hemicelluloses of lignocelluloses, and the xylose- and alkali-tolerant β-xylosidase with high catalytic activity is very attractive for promoting enzymatic hydrolysis of alkaline-pretreated lignocellulose. In this study, a novel intracellular glycoside hydrolase family 43 β-xylosidase gene (xyl43) from Penicillium oxalicum 114-2 was successfully high-level overexpressed in Pichia pastoris, and the secreted enzyme was characterized. The β-xylosidase Xyl43 exhibited great pH stability and high catalytic activity in the range of pH 6.0 to 8.0, and high tolerance to xylose with the Ki value of 28.09 mM. The Xyl43 could effectively promote enzymatic degradation of different source of xylan and hemicellulose contained in alkaline-pretreated corn stover, and high conversion of xylan to xylose could be obtained.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
